/**
 * The one door from the canvas's ES modules to Moodle's AMD modules.
 *
 * A component cannot import an AMD module: the import map Moodle serves resolves `@moodle/lms/`,
 * react and react-dom, and nothing of RequireJS, so `import Ajax from 'core/ajax'` in a .tsx fails
 * to resolve in the browser and the canvas never mounts. AMD is reached through core's loader
 * (`@moodle/lms/core/amd`) instead, and only from this file. Every module the canvas may load is a
 * key of `Modules`, so any other name is a type error under the tsc gate; the hub's dialogues are
 * reached here and never copied. Strings and the pending counter are core's ES modules
 * (`@moodle/lms/core/stringUtils`, `@moodle/lms/core/pending`) and are imported, not bridged.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/amd
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * A left-to-right tidy tree: the root at the left, one column per depth.
 *
 * Every leaf takes the next row, in the order given, and every parent sits level with the middle
 * of its first and last child, so subtrees never overlap and siblings keep the server's order. A
 * gap after each top-level subtree that has children keeps the framework's areas apart. Pure: no
 * library and no DOM, so Jest pins it; positions are the top-left corners React Flow places nodes by.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/layout
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * The lazily loaded tree the canvas draws: which competencies are known, which branches are loaded
 * and which are open.
 *
 * Pure and immutable: every function returns a new tree and leaves its argument alone, so React
 * state holds it as it is and Jest reads it without a DOM. A branch is the loaded part of a
 * parent's direct children, in the server's sort order, with the parent's total beside it: fewer
 * ids than the total means more pages to load.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/tree
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * From the tree to what React Flow draws: one node per visible competency, the framework at the
 * left, a "load more" node after a partly loaded branch, the parent-child edges and, for the
 * selected competency, a dotted edge to each related competency on the canvas.
 *
 * Pure: the nodes carry plain data, and the components read the callbacks from context.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/graph
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * Escaping for the few strings the canvas hands to an HTML sink of core's (a dialogue's title or
 * question), and the check an admin colour passes before it reaches a style.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/html
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * The canvas's strings: read once at mount, then filled in place.
 *
 * The page hands every one of them to core's string cache (hubv2_page::STRINGS and OTHER_STRINGS,
 * through strings_for_js), so {@see loadLabels()} resolves without a request. hubv2_page_test holds
 * these lists equal to the server's and every key present in both languages.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/strings
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * The HTML of the two deletion dialogues: why a competency cannot be deleted, and what deleting it destroys.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/deletion
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * The canvas's node cards and its rule edge.
 *
 * React Flow wraps each card in a focusable element (role group, named by the competency, Enter or
 * Space selects it); the card itself holds the one control a node has of its own, the button that
 * opens or closes its children, which stops its key and click from also selecting the node.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/Nodes
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * The panel beside the canvas: the selected competency's details and actions, or the framework's
 * when nothing is selected, and the controls of the move mode while it lasts.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/Panel
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * Holds on Moodle's pending-JavaScript counter across the canvas's asynchronous gaps.
 *
 * core/ajax holds the counter only while a request is in flight; a chain of requests separated by
 * a React render (children loaded, state changed, the layout recomputed, the node centred) leaves
 * a gap Behat would read as a settled page. Each gap is spanned by one `local_dimensions/hubv2:<what>`
 * token from start to the last state change.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/pending
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * The only module of the canvas that talks to the server: the hub's own web services and core's
 * competency services, called with the arguments the hub's list view passes
 * (amd/src/central/structure.js).
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/repository
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * The tree's search: a field, and its hits in a list under it. Choosing a hit reveals it on the
 * canvas (its ancestors opened, loading as needed), selects it and centres it.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/Search
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
/**
 * Competency hub v2: a framework's tree as a canvas of nodes, with a detail panel beside it.
 *
 * The entry of the bundle (js/esm/bundle.json), mounted by templates/hubv2.mustache with the props
 * classes/output/hubv2_page.php builds. The tree is lazy: the first page of roots arrives as props,
 * each branch is loaded when it is first opened (local_dimensions_browse_structure), and a node is
 * refreshed from the server after every change. Nothing is persisted: the layout is recomputed from
 * the tree on every change (layout.ts), and nodes cannot be dragged. Every action reuses the hub's
 * own dialogues and core's competency services, called as the list view (amd/src/central/structure.js)
 * calls them.
 *
 * @module     local_dimensions/hubv2/Hub
 * @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
 * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
 */
